comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-01T14:41:40.376Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: all-status searches for scale budget, Node 26, shape-qualified tiers, stale baselines, and list/get token drift found the original harness pm-mi2x, fixed-runtime regression pm-hcrmye, transport ratchet pm-yse5dt, and output-budget roadmap pm-5t33or, but no item owns the combined legacy-key and current-contract baseline drift. Exact-main at ba9680239 and this branch produce identical list/get bytes and comparable startup/RSS, so this is not introduced by the active context implementation."
  "2026-09-01T15:48:15.679Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence 2026-09-01: the legacy scratch tier is now shape-qualified as scratch:10000. Clean exact-main ba9680239 and delivery-head Node 24 five-iteration reports produced identical payload contracts and no product failures. The committed observations use the documented 25% headroom methodology. Head-minus-main minimum latency deltas were CLI list -8ms, get +7ms, next +62ms, context +47ms, search -2ms, create +4ms, claim +13ms; SDK list +2ms, get +17ms, next +62ms, context +91ms, search +56ms, create +4ms, claim +6ms. Every measurement remains below the published 1000ms p95 and 5000-token product ceilings. The unmodified three-iteration Node 24 check passed and wrote .cache/scale-node24-final-report.json. Node 26 variance was treated as non-baseline diagnostic evidence, not a feature regression."
